<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n577" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκύλ-η</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], ἡ, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰγκος</span>) properly, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκάλη</span>
			, <i>bend of the arm</i> or <i>wrist,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ̓ ἀγκύλης ἱέναι,</span> a phrase
			descriptive of the way in which the cottabus was thrown, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				13.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ̓ ἀγκύλης ζησι λάταγας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					273
				</span></i>
			; wrongly expl. as <i>cup,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.782d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bend of the knee, ham,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.6
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.726
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>joint bent and stiffened by disease,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Liqu.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.196
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>loop, noose,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλεκτὰς ἀγκύλας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1408
				</span></i>
			; in the leash of a hound, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				6.1
			</span></i>; in bandages, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(1).790
			</span></i>; in torsion-engines, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Bel.</u>
				83.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>thong of a javelin,</i> by which it was hurled, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				4.4.3
			</span></i>; hence, <i>the javelin</i> itself, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1476
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Phil.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἀγκυλῶν ἱππόται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Them.
					<u>Or.</u>
					21.256d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>bow-string,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. χρυσόστροΦοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					203
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκύλη τῆς ἐμβάδος</span>
				sandal-<i>thong,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>curtain-ring, hook,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				38.18
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				36.34
			</span></i>), al.; <i>hook</i> for a door, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				11(2).165.11
			</span></i>, al. (Delos, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>6.</b>
			<i>sides of the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεραία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.91
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
